            "notes": "## Powers  \n\nIn most games I take [Quantum Clip](item_3a108115-ec6e-4b98-8074-1b015cf535f1). It's simply more ammo, which means we can ramp up the attack speed.\n\n## Items  \n\n[Stockpile](item_a113eb56-9999-4f22-9bd7-18f4dbd00cc2) and [Pulse Detector](item_79ddef46-8917-4d8f-a123-7ddb589ad3e7) are excellent picks since they both scale [Foresight](item_f4163ce1-8f80-43ca-85d4-39812084400f) and increase [Attack Speed](stat_attack_speed). For poorer rounds, just keep [Ammo Reserves](item_982d53aa-5ef4-493f-93e7-9e374d0ebf34) over [Stockpile](item_a113eb56-9999-4f22-9bd7-18f4dbd00cc2).\n\n[Aftermarket Firing Pin](item_2485b212-b286-42d0-a2bd-20eb4396b054) is not that important \u2014you can keep [Compensator](item_2a354f80-610c-4661-9bdd-8960ae1a60b0) and barely lose any damage.\n\nIf there are many armor targets, consider picking up [Codebreaker](item_caa96c7e-655f-4d03-9bd9-0f41937fec27), since armor cuts your damage in half.\n\nIf you have slots already filled, you might as well just buy [Weapon Jammer](item_72386db6-753e-413d-aa2a-f1389842f47f).",
